    a0^alpha c^beta G^gamma = a length  =>  (alpha,beta,gamma) = (-1.0000,+2.0000,-0.0000); null space dimension 0
  [PASS] L1 the length A5's operator must use is UNIQUE (no free family), i.e. f(-D^2/a0^2) has one scale   (it is l0 = c^2/a0; G cannot enter without a mass, so no other length exists)
    canonical: a0 = 9.3619e-11 m/s^2  ->  l0 = c^2/a0 = 9.6001e+26 m = 31.11 Gpc  (Hubble radius c/H0 = 4.45 Gpc)
    alternate: a0 = 1.1279e-10 m/s^2  ->  l0 = c^2/a0 = 7.9684e+26 m = 25.82 Gpc  (Hubble radius c/H0 = 4.45 Gpc)

