5. F -- THE FILTERED GATE: A5-F, PAPER4's placement with xi -> l0 = c^2/a0
    Gaussian filter S = e^{xi^2 Delta/2}: for a point mass S u = -GM erf(r/(sqrt2 xi))/r, so
        |grad(S u)|(r) = GM | erf(x)/r^2 - sqrt(2/pi) e^{-x^2}/(xi r) |,  x = r/(sqrt2 xi),
    which tends to GM/r^2 for x >> 1 and to 0.2660 GM r/xi^3 for x << 1 (the smoothed cloud's interior).
  [PASS] C4 [control] at PAPER4's own filter length xi = 0.03 pc the filter is inert at 20 kpc   (|grad(S u)|/|grad u| = 1.000000000000)
  [PASS] C5 [control] both filter shapes reproduce their analytic interior limits and are inert at PAPER4's xi   (Gaussian interior sqrt(2)/(3 sqrt(pi)): 0.26594 vs 0.26596; Helmholtz interior GM/(2 xi^2): ratio 0.999968; Helmholtz at xi = 0.03 pc: 1.000000000000)

    A5-F with xi = l0, evaluated on a 1e11 Msun galaxy at 20 kpc:
    canonical: unfiltered s = g_N/a0 = 0.3723 -> y = 0.7232, phantom = 3.285e-11 m/s^2
               filtered   s = 2.628e-20 -> y = 1.621e-10, phantom = 1.518e-20 m/s^2   (argument suppressed 1.42e+19x, phantom 2.16e+09x)
    alternate: unfiltered s = g_N/a0 = 0.3090 -> y = 0.6480, phantom = 3.823e-11 m/s^2
               filtered   s = 3.809e-20 -> y = 1.952e-10, phantom = 2.201e-20 m/s^2   (argument suppressed 8.11e+18x, phantom 1.74e+09x)
    canonical: suppression of |grad(S u)| at 20 kpc -- Gaussian 1.42e+19x, Helmholtz 4.84e+12x (both filter shapes PAPER4 names)
    alternate: suppression of |grad(S u)| at 20 kpc -- Gaussian 8.11e+18x, Helmholtz 3.33e+12x (both filter shapes PAPER4 names)
  [FAIL] F1 A5-F keeps the MOND argument within a factor 2 of its unfiltered value on galactic scales   (the a0-scaled filter suppresses |grad(S u)| by 1.42e+19 (Gaussian) and 4.84e+12 (Helmholtz) at 20 kpc -- it smooths the galaxy over 31 Gpc -- and the deep-MOND phantom by the square root of that. The two shapes differ by orders of magnitude and neither is remotely survivable: the MOND effect is not modified, it is annihilated)

    the opposite sign: a SHARPENING elliptic filter S^-1 = 1 - xi^2 Delta.  For an exponential
    disc (M_b = 6e10 Msun, R_d = 3 kpc, z_0 = 300 pc) S^-1 u = u - 4 pi G xi^2 rho, so
    canonical: rho(R=8.2 kpc) = 7.78e-21 kg/m^3, |grad rho| = 8.41e-40;  4 pi G xi^2 |grad rho| = 6.498e+05 m/s^2  =>  y = 6.941e+15
    alternate: rho(R=8.2 kpc) = 7.78e-21 kg/m^3, |grad rho| = 8.41e-40;  4 pi G xi^2 |grad rho| = 4.477e+05 m/s^2  =>  y = 3.969e+15
  [FAIL] F2 the sharpening filter at the a0 scale leaves y in the MOND range somewhere in a real disc   (y = 6.94e+15 inside the disc, so mu = 1 to machine precision and the theory is exactly Newtonian)

    the pincer: the window of filter lengths that are merely HARMLESS on a galaxy
    smoothing branch needs xi << r_gal ~ 20 kpc = 1.00e+04 pc
    sharpening branch needs xi << sqrt(a0/(4 pi G |grad rho|)) = 3.73e+02 pc
    PAPER4's Solar-System-fixed xi = 0.02-0.05 pc sits inside that window; l0 = 3.11e+10 pc is outside it by 8.33e+07
  [FAIL] F3 [pincer] SOME monotone filter at the a0 scale has its transition inside 1 Mpc   (both branches require xi below ~3.7e+02 pc; l0 exceeds that by 8.3e+07. Smoothing gives Newton by killing the argument, sharpening gives Newton by saturating it; there is no third sign)

6. D -- THE DOF GATE (I3a, G4, P4): an actual Hamiltonian count, controls first
    controls (textbook counts my machinery must reproduce before it is used on the candidate):
      free scalar                    n= 1  primary= 0  constraints= 0  (1st  0 / 2nd  0)  ->  DOF = 1.0   [want 1]
      scalar + Lagrange multiplier   n= 2  primary= 1  constraints= 4  (1st  0 / 2nd  4)  ->  DOF = 0.0   [want 0]
      Maxwell                        n= 4  primary= 1  constraints= 2  (1st  2 / 2nd  0)  ->  DOF = 2.0   [want 2]
      Proca                          n= 4  primary= 1  constraints= 2  (1st  0 / 2nd  2)  ->  DOF = 3.0   [want 3]
      ADM/Fierz-Pauli GR             n=10  primary= 4  constraints= 8  (1st  8 / 2nd  0)  ->  DOF = 2.0   [want 2]
      massive Fierz-Pauli            n=10  primary= 4  constraints=10  (1st  0 / 2nd 10)  ->  DOF = 5.0   [want 5]
  [PASS] C6 [control] the Dirac counter returns the textbook DOF on six known systems, including 2 for GR   (free scalar 1, scalar+multiplier 0, Maxwell 2, Proca 3, linearised GR 2, massive Fierz-Pauli 5)

    the candidate's own sector.  The filter is localised the only way it can be localised in an
    action, with an auxiliary w and a multiplier lam:  L_f = lam[(1 - l^2 Delta) w - u].
      spatial/elliptic   (1 - l^2 Delta): constraints=4 (1st 0 / 2nd 4)  ->  DOF = 0.0
      temporal           (1 - l^2 Box)  : constraints=0 (1st 0 / 2nd 0)  ->  DOF = 2.0, kinetic eigenvalues -2.0, +2.0 (one ghost)
      elliptic at a ZERO of the symbol   : constraints=2 (1st 2 / 2nd 0) -- the four second-class constraints degenerate; the auxiliary stops being determined by u
  [PASS] D1 [A5's central claim] the spatial elliptic localisation adds NO canonical initial data   (four second-class constraints (pi_w, pi_lam, (1-l^2 Delta)w - u, (1-l^2 Delta)lam) remove the pair exactly; this is the one part of A5 that is simply true, and it is true for any positive symbol)
  [PASS] D2 [P6 contrast] the SAME localisation with a temporal operator does add propagating modes, which is what makes P6 closed and A5 open   (it adds 2 with kinetic eigenvalues -2/+2 -- a ghost pair. P6's warning reproduced quantitatively from the same machinery that gives D1)
  [PASS] D3 [contrast] ellipticity is load-bearing in D1, i.e. the count changes at a zero of the symbol   (at a zero of the symbol the second-class quartet collapses to 2 first-class constraints: the auxiliary stops being determined by u and its evolution becomes undetermined. Positivity of the symbol, not the word 'auxiliary', is what makes D1 true (P4))

    the price A5 does not pay in D1: the filter needs a FOLIATION.  There is no covariant elliptic
    operator on a Lorentzian manifold -- D^2 built from g alone is Box, which is hyperbolic -- so
    'spatial' requires a unit timelike n_mu, i.e. a khronon tau with n_mu = -d_mu tau/|d tau|.
    Two toy Lagrangians settle whether the A5 term itself can pay for that khronon.  In unitary
    gauge the Stuckelberg field enters through the lapse, ln N ~ pi_dot:
      A5 term, N only in the measure  L = N sqrt(gamma) Q(gamma): pi_dot enters LINEARLY, kinetic matrix = 0.00  ->  khronon DOF = 0.0
      host's acceleration term        L = c14 (d_i ln N)^2      : kinetic matrix = 2 c14 k^2 = 0.60  ->  khronon DOF = 1.0
  [FAIL] D4 the A5 term supplies the kinetic normalisation of the foliation mode it requires   (the filter is built from gamma_ij alone and N appears only in the measure, so its khronon kinetic matrix is exactly ZERO. Either the host supplies c14 != 0 -- and then N_grav = 3, failing I3a -- or nothing does and the foliation scalar is infinitely strongly coupled, which is P7 verbatim. A5 is kinetically inert, and inertness is not the same as being free)
      => N_grav = 2 (tensor, control) + 0 (filter pair, D1) + 1 (the foliation the filter needs) = 3
  [FAIL] D5 [I3a] the A5 construction delivers exactly two gravitational modes   (3. The count is 2 only if the foliation is a NON-DYNAMICAL background structure, which is not a diffeomorphism-invariant theory; with a dynamical khronon it is 3, the same count the lead's parallel construction has (L4_VERIFICATION.md). A5's 'no temporal mode' is true of the filter and false of the theory the filter has to live in)

