    canonical: M = 1e+11 Msun, g_N/a0 =  0.3723:  MOND boost =  1.943,   A5-L boost = 1.000000409248
    alternate: M = 1e+09 Msun, g_N/a0 =  0.0031:  MOND boost = 18.243,   A5-L boost = 1.000000493052
    alternate: M = 1e+11 Msun, g_N/a0 =  0.3090:  MOND boost =  2.097,   A5-L boost = 1.000000493052
  [FAIL] S1 [I4] the A5 modification is controlled by a local acceleration   (the two boosts are identical to 4.4e-16: a filter is triggered by a LENGTH (a wavenumber), never by an amplitude. This is I4's exact prohibition -- the trigger is a scale label, not a dynamical acceleration)
    canonical: A5-L anomalous sunward acceleration at Saturn = 6.142e-20 m/s^2 (repository gate 3.66e-14) -> 1.7e-06 of the bound
    alternate: A5-L anomalous sunward acceleration at Saturn = 7.400e-20 m/s^2 (repository gate 3.66e-14) -> 2.0e-06 of the bound
  [PASS] S2 [Solar System] A5-L passes the Solar-System gate   (it passes by six orders of magnitude, but VACUOUSLY: it passes for the same reason it fails the MOND gate -- the modification is ~1e-16 of Newton everywhere inside 1 Mpc. A gate that a theory passes by doing nothing is not evidence of screening)

